mkdir makes the directory: yes
open O_DIRECTORY opens a directory: yes
fstat of it is a directory: yes
read of it is EISDIR: yes
open O_DIRECTORY of a file is ENOTDIR: yes
mkdirat makes a directory in it: yes
openat opens it: yes
openat makes a file from it: yes
fstatat finds the file from the parent: yes
the file has one name: yes
fstatat with AT_EMPTY_PATH is the descriptor's own: yes
fstatat of the empty path without it is ENOENT: yes
a path from a descriptor that is no directory is ENOTDIR: yes
fstatat of a bad descriptor is EBADF: yes
an absolute path ignores the descriptor: yes
a `..` from the directory climbs to its parent: yes
a `..` above the directory's root is EACCES: yes
an empty path from a descriptor is ENOENT: yes
the directory is still there: yes
open of the empty path is ENOENT: yes
symlinkat makes a link from the descriptor: yes
readlinkat reads it: yes
fstatat follows it: yes
fstatat AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW is the link: yes
unlinkat of a directory without AT_REMOVEDIR is refused: yes
renameat moves the file to the parent: yes
the file is in the parent's listing: yes
renameat moves the directory: yes
its descriptor follows it: yes
unlinkat AT_REMOVEDIR of a full directory is ENOTEMPTY: yes
unlinkat AT_REMOVEDIR removes an empty one: yes
unlinkat removes the link: yes
dirfd answers the stream's descriptor: yes
link is ENOTSUP: yes
linkat is ENOTSUP: yes
O_TMPFILE is ENOTSUP: yes
O_TMPFILE to read alone is EINVAL: yes
utimensat sets the modification time: yes
stat reads it back to the nanosecond: yes
futimens sets it through a descriptor: yes
fstat reads that back: yes
UTIME_NOW sets it to now: yes
a tv_nsec past a second is EINVAL: yes
an access time the volume keeps none of is ENOTSUP: yes
O_DIRECTORY of a /tmp file is ENOTDIR: yes
O_DIRECTORY of /tmp to write is EISDIR: yes
opendir of a /tmp file is ENOTDIR: yes
utimes of the kernel's /tmp is ENOTSUP: yes
pread beside a read on /home: yes
pread beside a read on /tmp: yes
pwrite at its offset on /home: yes
pwrite at its offset on /tmp: yes
pwrite beside a write on /home: yes
pwrite beside a write on /tmp: yes
pread of a negative offset is EINVAL: yes
rmdir removes the moved directory: yes
rmdir removes the directory: yes
